                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ed06c43-2e11-4840-bd16-0d301b9a78a3",
                                                "sense_id": "cdc32f0c-467b-3809-a84a-036f0e280d68",
                                                "text": "to be bricked alive (as a form of capital punishment)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd84e345-25d0-4db7-a564-e4a92fd73dc4",
                                                "sense_id": "cdc32f0c-467b-3809-a84a-036f0e280d68",
                                                "text": "If the ground is strong right up to the surface, a few yards are usually sunk and bricked before the engines and pit top are erected"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93de0136-0042-4c24-a9f8-ee12dce4bc33",
                                                "sense_id": "cdc32f0c-467b-3809-a84a-036f0e280d68",
                                                "text": "The shaft was next bricked between the decks until the top scaffold was supported by the brickwork and [made] to share the weight with the prids."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95deca70-965e-4840-82b8-7f3048f10a02",
                                                "sense_id": "cdc32f0c-467b-3809-a84a-036f0e280d68",
                                                "text": "He came in and we went out to the back area I'd bricked amateurishly years ago."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8d60186-7595-3d4e-aa0e-b61f464d4754",
                                        "entry_id": "36ee9734-2368-398b-95dd-e5331a87290e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make into bricks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40ffa394-3f45-4198-943d-5f418f29dcea",
                                                "sense_id": "a8d60186-7595-3d4e-aa0e-b61f464d4754",
                                                "text": "The plant, which is here described, for bricking fine ores and flue dust, was designed and the plans produced in the engineering department of the Selby smelter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a289aa6-f1ec-3249-abc9-0deff444c5ea",
                                        "entry_id": "36ee9734-2368-398b-95dd-e5331a87290e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hit someone or something with a brick."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c68afbc5-2cea-383c-b15b-0eb9b048cea4",
                                        "entry_id": "36ee9734-2368-398b-95dd-e5331a87290e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (an electronic device) non-functional and usually beyond repair, as a result of software or configuration issues."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fad8dab9-4f56-4a24-a88e-3f233cce3ab1",
                                                "sense_id": "c68afbc5-2cea-383c-b15b-0eb9b048cea4",
                                                "text": "My VCR was bricked during the lightning storm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3285138f-9f7d-4c68-8f59-ca6567669935",
                                                "sense_id": "c68afbc5-2cea-383c-b15b-0eb9b048cea4",
                                                "text": "Just need to project against users from deleting NK.BIN and bricking the device."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92813c0e-5f44-433d-824b-d89cd6a14eb5",
                                                "sense_id": "c68afbc5-2cea-383c-b15b-0eb9b048cea4",
                                                "text": "installing third-party firmware will void your warranty, and it is possible that you may brick your router."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f7ca061-0199-4d31-bf8e-9c140c5cfc21",
                                                "sense_id": "c68afbc5-2cea-383c-b15b-0eb9b048cea4",
                                                "text": "Google owner Alphabet’s subsidiary Nest is closing a smart-home company it bought less than two years ago, leaving customers’ devices useless as of May. […] The company declined to share how many customers would be left with bricked devices as a result of the shutdown."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97183213-5510-35f0-be9d-f35315c92fcf",
                                        "entry_id": "36ee9734-2368-398b-95dd-e5331a87290e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an electronic device, to become non-functional, especially in a way beyond repair, as a result of software or configuration issues."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46f5e23c-96d1-4f55-81c7-df9e9535a4ce",
                                                "sense_id": "97183213-5510-35f0-be9d-f35315c92fcf",
                                                "text": "My phone bricked halfway through the videoconference."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba017947-c1b7-339d-a3d5-aa81089b69d3",
                                        "entry_id": "36ee9734-2368-398b-95dd-e5331a87290e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To blunder; to screw up."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "brick",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2481b1d0-c743-3e48-a508-13db7c32f5fe",
                                        "entry_id": "01d6ced4-89ab-38de-ae9d-133f04fe732d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Extremely cold."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "New-York",
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f396b71b-5ba4-4cdc-a225-3d16de995a6c",
                                                "sense_id": "2481b1d0-c743-3e48-a508-13db7c32f5fe",
                                                "text": "And while the tropics are definitely the place to be when it's brick outside, rocking a snorkel on the beach only works when you're snorkeling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61965c79-51e6-4431-9b08-c393dc03a3b0",
                                                "sense_id": "2481b1d0-c743-3e48-a508-13db7c32f5fe",
                                                "text": "He was always hanging tight with me and since he had access to a ride . . . it made traveling easier. I mean it was no biggie brain buster to take the train, but when it's brick outside . . . fuck the A train."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2203328-b84c-4290-a8a1-6c7864c73774",
                                                "sense_id": "2481b1d0-c743-3e48-a508-13db7c32f5fe",
                                                "text": "Read on for tips so you don't freeze your ass off when it's brick outside."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed9718b4-cd58-4f79-8205-ea0855f8f2e5",
                                                "sense_id": "2481b1d0-c743-3e48-a508-13db7c32f5fe",
                                                "text": "\"It's brick cold. Could you imagine stepping on this with your bare foot?\" Taylor said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
